        "original_id": "7ef57d61-ac06-59d8-bc07-c53d3cf2a72e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Encore Las Vegas, Wynn Las Vegas, Las Vegas Strip, Paradise, Nevada, North Las Vegas, Las Vegas\n- Companies: Wynn Resorts\n- People: Steve Wynn, Tom Fazio, Carolyn Goodman\n- Roles: mayor, casino developer, real estate businessman, art collector\n- Properties: Shadow Creek Golf Course\n\nFacts:\n- In 1989, Steve Wynn built Shadow Creek, an 18-hole golf course in North Las Vegas, Nevada, and Tom Fazio designed it.\n- Steve Wynn, born Stephen Alan Wynn on January 27, 1942, is an American real estate businessman and art collector.\n- Carolyn Goodman has served as the mayor of Las Vegas, Nevada since 2011.\n- Encore Las Vegas is a luxury resort, casino, and hotel on the Las Vegas Strip in Paradise, Nevada.\n- Encore Las Vegas is also called Encore at Wynn Las Vegas or simply Encore.\n- Encore Las Vegas is connected to Wynn Las Vegas, its sister resort.\n- Wynn Resorts owns both Encore Las Vegas and Wynn Las Vegas.\n- Steve Wynn heads Wynn Resorts as a casino developer.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "b792275a-b033-50d4-9b77-a42bdec61e84",
        "text": "Page: Encore Las Vegas. Sentence: Encore Las Vegas (also called Encore at Wynn Las Vegas; often just called Encore) is a luxury resort, casino and hotel located on the Las Vegas Strip in Paradise, Nevada.\nPage: Encore Las Vegas. Sentence: The resort is connected to its sister resort, Wynn Las Vegas; both are owned by Wynn Resorts, headed by casino developer Steve Wynn.\nPage: Steve Wynn. Sentence: Stephen Alan Wynn (\"né\" Weinberg; born January 27, 1942) is an American real estate businessman and art collector.\nPage: Shadow Creek Golf Course. Sentence: Shadow Creek is an 18-hole golf course in North Las Vegas, Nevada, designed by Tom Fazio and built by Las Vegas casino magnate Steve Wynn in 1989.\nPage: Carolyn Goodman (politician). Sentence: She has been the mayor of Las Vegas, Nevada since 2011.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
